<html>
<title>Memory Type Selection</title>
<body>


<h1>Memory Type Selection</h1>


<h2>Automatic</h2>

<p>
Emma 02 will automatically set the correct memory type as long as the code has been executed since the emulator was started. Therefore, to view disassembled code, make sure the code has been executed first.
</p>


<h2>Manual</h2>

<p>
To change the type manually, use the marking interface shown below:
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/assembler_mark.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>One</strong> / <strong>Range</strong> selector</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Start</strong> location text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>End</strong> location text field</li>
<li>(4) <strong>Type</strong> choice button</li>
<li>(5) <strong>Mark</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
Follow these steps:
</p>
<ol>
<li>Select either <strong>One</strong> or <strong>Range</strong> (1) depending on whether one location or a range of locations need to be changed.</li>
<li>Fill in the <strong>Start</strong> location (2) to be changed; by default, this is the current working location.</li>
<li>Fill in the <strong>End</strong> location (3) if <strong>Range</strong> was selected.</li>
<li>Select the desired type via the <strong>Type</strong> choice button (4).</li>
<li>Press <strong>Mark</strong> (5).</li>
</ol>

<p>
In the example above, pressing <strong>Mark</strong> will mark address 0014 as <strong>1802</strong> code, which is already its current type and results in no change.
</p>

<p>
To save type information, see the <a href="DirectConfiguration.htm">Program Configuration</a> section.
</p>


<h2>Types</h2>

<p>
The following type choices are available:
</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>1802</strong>: SYSTEM00, RCA 1801, 1802, 1804, or 1805 code</li>
<li><strong>Data</strong>: data values</li>
<li><strong>Text</strong>: ASCII text</li>
<li><strong>Branch</strong>: 16 bit branch address (order: high byte - low byte), see <a href="DirectBranchData.htm">Branch Data</a></li>
<li><strong>Rev Br</strong>: 16 bit branch address (order: low byte - high byte), see <a href="DirectBranchData.htm">Reversed Branch Data</a></li>
<li><strong>LDL</strong>: LDL macro, see <a href="DirectLdl.htm">LDL, LDRL, LDV and RLDL Instructions</a></li>
<li><strong>LDRL</strong>: LDRL macro, see <a href="DirectLdl.htm">LDL, LDRL, LDV and RLDL Instructions</a></li>
<li><strong>LDV</strong>: LDV macro, see <a href="DirectLdl.htm">LDL, LDRL, LDV and RLDL Instructions</a></li>
<li><strong>Switch</strong>: Switch to another mnemonic, see <a href="DirectMnemonic.htm">Switch Mnemonic</a></li>
<li><strong>Pseudo</strong>: Pseudo-code, see <a href="SyntaxPseudoCode.htm">Pseudo Code</a></li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>